{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "P51828", "secondaryAccessions": ["A0AVA6"], "uniProtkbId": "ADCY7_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1996-10-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1996-10-01", "entryVersion": 197, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Adenylate cyclase type 7"}, "ecNumbers": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18541530"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23229509"}], "value": "4.6.1.1"}]}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "ATP pyrophosphate-lyase 7"}}, {"fullName": {"value": "Adenylate cyclase type VII"}}, {"fullName": {"value": "Adenylyl cyclase 7"}}, {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Cyclic di-AMP synthase ADCY7"}, "ecNumbers": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P51829"}], "value": "2.7.7.85"}]}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "HGNC", "id": "HGNC:238"}], "value": "ADCY7"}, "synonyms": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "7584026"}], "value": "KIAA0037"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P51829"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11113152"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18541530"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23229509"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23842570"}], "value": "Adenylate cyclase that mediates formation of both cyclic AMP (cAMP) and cyclic di-AMP (c-di-AMP) (PubMed:11113152, PubMed:18541530, PubMed:23229509). Acts as a key mediator of G protein-coupled receptor signaling by catalyzing the formation of cAMP downstream of G protein-coupled receptors (PubMed:18541530, PubMed:23229509). Functions in G protein-coupled receptor signaling cascades activated by thrombin, sphingosine 1-phosphate, dopamine and anaphylatoxin C5a (PubMed:18541530, PubMed:23229509, PubMed:23842570). Mediates regulation of cAMP synthesis through synergistic action of the G alpha protein G(s) (GNAS) with G(13) (GNA13) (PubMed:18541530, PubMed:23229509). Also involved in inflammation by acting as a diadenylate cyclase that catalyzes the condensation of 2 ATP molecules into c-di-AMP (By similarity). Following activation by TLR9, mediates formation of c-di-AMP, which directly activates NLRP3, thereby promoting assembly and maturation of the NLRP3 inflammasome (By similarity). It is also required for the optimal functions of B- and T cells during adaptive immune responses by regulating cAMP synthesis in both B- and T-cells (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "ATP = 3',5'-cyclic AMP + diphosphate", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:15389"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:30616"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:33019"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:58165"}], "ecNumber": "4.6.1.1", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11113152"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18541530"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23229509"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "2 ATP = 3',3'-c-di-AMP + 2 diphosphate", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:35655"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:30616"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:33019"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:71500"}], "ecNumber": "2.7.7.85", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P51829"}]}, "physiologicalReactions": [{"directionType": "left-to-right", "reactionCrossReference": {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:35656"}, "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P51829"}]}]}, {"commentType": "COFACTOR", "cofactors": [{"name": "Mg(2+)", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P30803"}], "cofactorCrossReference": {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:18420"}}, {"name": "Mn(2+)", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P30803"}], "cofactorCrossReference": {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29035"}}], "note": {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P30803"}], "value": "Binds 2 magnesium ions per subunit. Is also active with manganese (in vitro)."}]}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P51829"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12454008"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18541530"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23229509"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Activated by G(s) G alpha protein (GNAS) (PubMed:18541530). Inhibited by G(i) G alpha protein GNAI1 (Probable). Activated by GNA13 and GNA12 (PubMed:18541530, PubMed:23229509). Ethanol and phorbol 12,13-dibutanoate significantly potentiate adenylate cyclase activity generated in response to the activation of the prostanoid receptor by the agonist prostaglandin E1(1-) in a PKC-dependent manner (PubMed:12454008). Inhibited by lithium (By similarity). Activated by TLR9, promoting synthesis of cyclic di-AMP (c-di-AMP) (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "ACTIVITY REGULATION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P51829"}], "value": "Interacts with TLR9; leading to ADCY7 activation and synthesis of cyclic di-AMP (c-di-AMP)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"value": "Membrane", "id": "SL-0162"}, "topology": {"value": "Multi-pass membrane protein", "id": "SL-9909"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P26769"}], "value": "The protein contains two modules with six transmembrane helices each; both are required for catalytic activity. Isolated N-terminal or C-terminal guanylate cyclase domains have no catalytic activity, but when they are brought together, enzyme activity is restored. The active site is at the interface of the two domains. Both contribute substrate-binding residues, but the catalytic metal ions are bound exclusively via the N-terminal guanylate cyclase domain"}], "commentType": "DOMAIN"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12454008"}], "value": "Phosphorylated by PRKCD"}], "commentType": "PTM"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "PROSITE-ProRule", "id": "PRU00099"}], "value": "Belongs to the adenylyl cyclase class-4/guanylyl cyclase family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}, {"commentType": "SEQUENCE CAUTION", "sequenceCautionType": "Erroneous initiation", "sequence": "BAA05021.2", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}]}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 1080, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Adenylate cyclase type 7", "featureId": "PRO_0000195703"}, {"type": "Topological domain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 33, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Cytoplasmic", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}]}, {"type": "Transmembrane"